# Serply

> Serply is a REST API (and hosted MCP server) for live search-engine results and page scraping: Google Search, News, Maps, Images, Jobs, Scholar, Video, Bing, Amazon products, eBay, and Reddit as structured JSON, plus any URL as markdown or HTML. Built for developers and AI agents; prepaid credits, 2,500 free to start.

- Base URL: `https://api.serply.io`. Authenticate every request with an `X-Api-Key` header.
- Hosted MCP server: `https://api.serply.io/mcp` (same API key). Docs: https://serply.io/mcp.md
- Free tier: 2,500 credits on signup, no card, valid for 30 days. Sign up: https://app.serply.io/users/sign_up
- Billing: prepaid credit packs, no subscription. 1 credit = 1 successful uncached request; cached and failed requests are free. Purchased credits never expire.
- Location and device: optional `X-Proxy-Location` header picks one of 14 proxy regions (`US`, `EU`, `GB`, `DE`, `JP`, and others; see the endpoint docs) and `X-User-Agent` picks `desktop` (default) or `mobile`.
- Agent skill file (Claude/Agent Skills format): https://serply.io/skill.md

## APIs

- [Google Search API](https://serply.io/docs/resources/google-search.md): `GET /v1/search`. Organic Google results with search operators, site: filters, and date ranges. Overview: https://serply.io/google-search-api
- [Google News API](https://serply.io/docs/resources/google-news.md): `GET /v1/news`. Real-time Google News headlines and topic clusters. Overview: https://serply.io/google-news-api
- [Google Maps API](https://serply.io/docs/resources/google-maps.md): `GET /v1/maps/search`. Places with name, address, coordinates, rating, phone, and hours. Overview: https://serply.io/google-maps-api
- [Google Images API](https://serply.io/docs/resources/google-images.md): `GET /v1/image`. Image results with thumbnails, dimensions, and source URLs. Overview: https://serply.io/google-images-api
- [Google Jobs API](https://serply.io/docs/resources/google-jobs.md): `GET /v1/job/search`. Job listings with remote/hybrid flags, salary ranges, and benefits. Overview: https://serply.io/google-jobs-api
- [Google Scholar API](https://serply.io/docs/resources/google-scholar.md): `GET /v1/scholar`. Academic papers with citation counts and metadata. Overview: https://serply.io/google-scholar-api
- [Google Video API](https://serply.io/docs/resources/google-video.md): `GET /v1/video`. Video results with duration, view counts, and channel data. Overview: https://serply.io/google-video-api
- [Bing Search API](https://serply.io/docs/resources/bing-search.md): `GET /v1/b/search`. Bing results, including ads and shopping ads Google does not return. Overview: https://serply.io/bing-search-api
- [Product Search API (Amazon)](https://serply.io/docs/resources/google-product.md): `GET /v1/product/search`. Amazon listings with ASIN, price, Prime eligibility, and bestseller status. Overview: https://serply.io/google-product-api
- [eBay Search API](https://serply.io/docs/resources/ebay.md): `GET /v1/ebay/search`. eBay listings with price, condition, seller feedback, and shipping. Overview: https://serply.io/ebay-api
- [Reddit API](https://serply.io/docs/resources/reddit.md): `GET /v1/reddit/{subreddit,post,user,comments}`. Subreddit listings, posts, user history, and comment threads, no OAuth. Overview: https://serply.io/reddit-api
- [Web Scraping API](https://serply.io/docs/resources/requests.md): `POST /v1/request`. Any URL as clean markdown or raw HTML, CAPTCHAs handled. Overview: https://serply.io/web-scraping-api

## Pricing

- [Pricing](https://serply.io/pricing.md): Prepaid credit packs from $5, free tier, and how credits are counted

## Guides

- [Introduction](https://serply.io/docs/guides/introduction.md): Serply API documentation - perform web searches and gather real-time market data. Search Google, Bing, News, and Products with JSON responses and geo-targeting.
- [Quickstart](https://serply.io/docs/guides/quickstart.md): Get started with Serply API in minutes. Learn how to make your first Google Search API request with code examples in JavaScript, Python, and cURL.
- [MCP Server](https://serply.io/mcp.md): Connect Claude, Cursor, or any MCP client to the hosted Serply MCP server - fourteen tools for live Google Search, Bing, News, Scholar, Maps, Reddit, and web scraping. One config line, nothing to deploy.
- [SDKs](https://serply.io/docs/guides/sdks.md): Serply API code examples and integration guides for JavaScript, Python, cURL, C#, and Java. Get started quickly with our example code repository.
- [Authentication](https://serply.io/docs/guides/authentication.md): Learn how to authenticate Serply API requests using your API key. Includes security best practices, rate limits, and example code for secure API integration.
- [Pagination](https://serply.io/docs/guides/pagination.md): Page through Serply API search results using the num and start parameters. How page size is capped, how to detect the last page, and how billing works per request.
- [Errors](https://serply.io/docs/guides/errors.md): Understand Serply API error responses, HTTP status codes, and rate limits. Learn how to handle errors gracefully with JavaScript and Python code examples.
- [Webhooks](https://serply.io/docs/guides/webhooks.md): The Serply REST API does not offer outbound webhooks. How to get near-real-time results by polling instead, and why cached responses make it inexpensive.
- [Google Search Operators](https://serply.io/docs/guides/search-operators)
- [Agent Skill](https://serply.io/docs/guides/agent-skill.md): Install the Serply Agent Skill so Claude and other Skill-compatible agents know how to call the Serply API and MCP server without re-explaining it every session.
- [Strands Agents](https://serply.io/docs/guides/strands.md): Give a Strands Agents agent live Google Search, Scholar, News, Maps, Reddit and page scraping by pointing its MCPClient at the hosted Serply MCP server with one header.

For the full text of every page in one file, see https://serply.io/llms-full.txt